│  1 What does this part of the code do?                             │
│                                                                    │
│ The format_chunk method processes different kinds of events        │
│ received from the Ollama model streaming interface and converts    │
│ them into a standardized message chunk format used internally. It  │
│ handles different chunk types such as "message_start",             │
│ "content_start", "content_delta", "content_stop", "message_stop",  │
│ and "metadata". Specifically, for the "metadata" chunk type, it    │
│ extracts usage details including inputTokens, outputTokens,        │
│ totalTokens, and latency metrics from the event's data.            │
│                                                                    │
│  2 What is the relationship between this part of the code and the  │
│    bug?                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ This method, specifically the section handling the "metadata"      │
│ chunk type, is exactly where the bug lies. The issue is that the   │
│ inputTokens and outputTokens are swapped, i.e.,                    │
│ event["data"].eval_count is used as inputTokens and                │
│ event["data"].prompt_eval_count is used as outputTokens, which is  │
│ the opposite of what Ollama's API documentation specifies.         │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│                                                                    │
│ The intended behavior is to correctly assign inputTokens to        │
│ event["data"].prompt_eval_count and outputTokens to                │
│ event["data"].eval_count, so the reported token counts align with  │
│ the true number of tokens in the prompt and the model’s output     │
│ respectively. The totalTokens value should remain the sum of these │
│ two. All other functionality in the method should be preserved     │
│ unchanged.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ This analysis confirms the exact fix needed: swapping the two      │
│ assignments for "inputTokens" and "outputTokens" in the "metadata" │
│ chunk case of format_chunk.                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ No additional code outside this method/class currently seems       │
│ critical to review for the fix.                                    │
